{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552297-what-do-people-get-wrong-about-vtm","id":1552297,"title":"What do people get wrong about VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-11T21:53:16-07:00","id":1552297,"title":"What do people get wrong about VTM?","content":"This was inspired by Warhammer 40 K youtuber General Bradley VA101 on what people get wrong about the lore and legions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T00:45:37-07:00","id":1552298,"title":"","content":"Who?<br /> The players and Story tellers or everyone else?<br /> If the former then the question is irrelevant, there is no &quot;wrong way&quot; to interpret and play, you can't really get wrong Vampire (aka. the Golden Rule - if you don't like it, change it, leave it out ,etc, it is your game, the point is to have fun)<br /> If the later? Vampires neither sparkle nor the game is an Anne Rice book sequel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T02:53:28-07:00","id":1552299,"title":"","content":"A somewhat similar but different approach to Shadeprowler's response:<br /> <br /> That there even is a correct lore of VtM. VtM is supposed to by mysterious and the vast majority of the lore is told by unreliable narrators with specific agendas. Dedicated fans of the game might have a consensus idea of what we can interpret the lore of a given edition was in the heads of the authors, but purposefully VtM is a game where the answers aren't clear cut and what the truth is can vary from ST to ST, table to table, group to group, without anyone actually being &quot;wrong.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T13:06:37-07:00","id":1552311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552297-what-do-people-get-wrong-about-vtm?p=1552299#post1552299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat similar but different approach to Shadeprowler's response:<br /> <br /> That there even is a correct lore of VtM. VtM is supposed to by mysterious and the vast majority of the lore is told by unreliable narrators with specific agendas. Dedicated fans of the game might have a consensus idea of what we can interpret the lore of a given edition was in the heads of the authors, but purposefully VtM is a game where the answers aren't clear cut and what the truth is can vary from ST to ST, table to table, group to group, without anyone actually being &quot;wrong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Can not agree more.<br /> <br /> Unreliable narrator is also a convenient form of explaining all the inconsistencies in the lore. Most of the people were not lying, they said or wrote as good as they knew, but did they have the correct information?<br /> <br /> That alone can give a ST material to take the narrative to wherever you want. It aligns beautifully with the Golden Rule. And this applies to ALL the gamelines not just Vampire, Vampire happens to be special in that a large number of those misinformed people from ancient times are still around, and their biases still colour the world they want to see and the way they interpretate new information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T21:14:24-07:00","id":1552342,"title":"","content":"I was referring to people who don't know much beyond the basics of the setting vtm and have a poor understanding of the clans and what they stand for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T22:17:22-07:00","id":1552347,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone expects vampires to sparkle outside <b>Twilight</b>, nor do I think it bad that they do there. I actually like <b>Twilight</b>'s worldbuilding proposal, as badly written as it is.<br /> <br /> What I personally think is the most common misconception, while not terribly wrong, is the idea that Vampire (or any horror setting for that matter) is Grim Dark. Gothic Punk isn't Grim Dark. Hope is an integral part of the game. It was downplayed with passing editions to broaden the options for STs, but the idea of darkness being unavoidable actually runs counter both Gothic and Punk literature.<br /> <br /> But isn't a terrible misconception. If that's what floats your boat, go for it, and in the end this darker take (if not necessarily all the way to Grim Dark) is more popular (hence the changes through editions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T22:24:36-07:00","id":1552348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552297-what-do-people-get-wrong-about-vtm?p=1552342#post1552342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to people who don't know much beyond the basics of the setting vtm and have a poor understanding of the clans and what they stand for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people don't, differently from what happens in Warhammer, at least in my experience. The clans are actually pretty easy to grasp most of the time, and the basic of their lore can be summed up in a single page. Even their &quot;ancient&quot; lore is quite simple, what is more thorough and complex is their DA lore, but then complete ignorance is far more common than misconceptions.<br /> <br /> If there's any actual misconception about the clans, in particular, I think it's just that the Banu Haqim isn't just a bunch of Arab Ninjas, but that's a problem mostly because their presentation in the core is actually like that, and the clan was heavily retconned (for better) in more obscure books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T22:38:53-07:00","id":1552349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552297-what-do-people-get-wrong-about-vtm?p=1552347#post1552347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone expects vampires to sparkle outside <b>Twilight</b>, nor do I think it bad that they do there. I actually like <b>Twilight</b>'s worldbuilding proposal, as badly written as it is.<br /> <br /> What I personally think is the most common misconception, while not terribly wrong, is the idea that Vampire (or any horror setting for that matter) is Grim Dark. Gothic Punk isn't Grim Dark. Hope is an integral part of the game. It was downplayed with passing editions to broaden the options for STs, but the idea of darkness being unavoidable actually runs counter both Gothic and Punk literature.<br /> <br /> But isn't a terrible misconception. If that's what floats your boat, go for it, and in the end this darker take (if not necessarily all the way to Grim Dark) is more popular (hence the changes through editions).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah a lot of time vtm (and vtr) writing leans into shitdark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T09:03:17-07:00","id":1552372,"title":"","content":"Well people keep insisting that VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE needs colours other than red when the setting clearly deserves to be rendered in nothing less than the finest Film Noir Black &amp; White with the occasional shock of Kensington gore \u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it\u2019s GOTHIC PUNK, not just plain Goth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T16:38:43-07:00","id":1552432,"title":"","content":"I think it's your world change what you want, get upset when people tell you. &quot;That didn't happen in the lore.&quot; Well, it did in this chronicle. I had a faction of Assamites joining the Camarilla back in a chronicle in the early 2000's and I had a player tell me. &quot;That will never happen.&quot; In short, it's your story tell what you want with your players and use established lore as you want or will,<br /> <br /> Also Rules Lawyers..... UGH","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1680,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","user":"Justicar-Seth","date":". 07-15-2025, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T06:45:14-07:00","id":1552486,"title":"","content":"I know that I was very restricted by the official lore when I came into VtM and WoD in general as a rookie. So maybe that's one of the things that people get wrong about any setting with extensive lore? Its not a straitjacket for your games but a set of suggestions for how you may develop your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T02:49:38-07:00","id":1552535,"title":"","content":"Something I recently clocked in vtm/wod writers struggle with intent of the work often relying on lazy slogans or reductive cliches. For example &quot;the ventrue want to rule whereas the lasombra want to win.&quot; Is ultimately a non statement which doesn't tell us anything or &quot;the sabbat in revised was just a dark reflection of the carmarilla&quot; which is proactively incorrect. This leads to issues with the writing as authors fail to understand other authors intent. <br /> <br /> <br /> With this in mind its unsurprising fans misunderstand the setting when its possible the authors don't. Like v5 being presented as a return to the 1st ed origin of the game when its got more in common with requiem and 3rd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T05:25:52-07:00","id":1552539,"title":"","content":"There's also the difference between how people played the game vs. what the game actually said. I think it's fair to say that V5 is intended in many ways a return to how some people (maybe even a lot of people that did so) played 1e and early 2e; even if it wasn't always strictly in-line with what the books themselves presented (esp. supplements). This certainly applies to authors as well (since any franchise as old as VtM has current authors that weren't playing the game when it first came out), but it's a bit different than just falling into non-statement traps.<br /> <br /> This is generally the ethos of the OSR style of games: use modern game design techniques to create games that lean into how early D&amp;D was played over directly iterating on the games via editions to try to dial in author and player communication. There's definitely a lot of good to be had in trying to refine a game from this perspective rather than the more traditional revision-over-time style that games generally have to do to last long enough to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T05:41:11-07:00","id":1552540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552297-what-do-people-get-wrong-about-vtm?p=1552299#post1552299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat similar but different approach to Shadeprowler's response:<br /> <br /> That there even is a correct lore of VtM. VtM is supposed to by mysterious and the vast majority of the lore is told by unreliable narrators with specific agendas. Dedicated fans of the game might have a consensus idea of what we can interpret the lore of a given edition was in the heads of the authors, but purposefully VtM is a game where the answers aren't clear cut and what the truth is can vary from ST to ST, table to table, group to group, without anyone actually being &quot;wrong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. I would replace &quot;correct&quot; with &quot;canon&quot; here.I'd say that since V5 have a targeted audience, which are not the old school fans (understandable, since their profit is expected elsewhere), this created a division. Some fans want the game as it was back in white-wolf times, V5 is not that. Other fans wants to exploit V5 potential and wish to keep the game as it currently is, I believe this is what Renegade/Paradox wants. Desiring a structured canon history is what old school fans want and I believe that's not gonna happen. That's what many fans of the VtM game get wrong.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T13:50:16-07:00","id":1552549,"title":"","content":"I mean, there is a canon lore, because canon just means the lore presented officially in the books and/or as recognized by the property owners (that is, Paradox can decanonize old official canon if they desire to). I feel like people can forget that canon doesn't inherently mean consistent or non-contradictory. One of the perceived advantages of unreliable narrators is that they can be wrong so you can adjust the lore-as-consumed by changed the character speaking (though many WoD contributors over the years have expressed serious concerns with how well that plays out given how many readers assume that the unreliable narrators are still communicating what the authors intend to be the official &quot;truth&quot; of the setting). There is canon lore that X NPC said various things on various topics, because their thoughts are presented officially in the texts. How accurately the NPCs are communicated the intent of the authors can be debated by fans, and altered by future writers.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's a good idea to dwell too much on divisions within the community, but I don't think it's as clear cut as you're saying. I'm in my third decade of playing WoD games (so I'm pretty sure I get to count as an &quot;old school fan&quot;) and I vastly prefer the CofD approach of a looser canonical history of the setting (though there is a lot more canon lore and history than is sometimes acknowledged) over the older approach the original WW took with the WoD. V5, esp. compared to H5 and W5, was written with far more desire to honor the old canon of the game without being strictly beholden to it.<br /> <br /> I also don't think most old school fans that dislike WoD5 are somehow wrong about where WoD5 is headed... where it's headed is largely why they don't like it. WoD5 is not what I want, and I'm extremely sure moving closer to what I want is not going to happen, so I'm not a WoD5 fan. Simple as that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T08:26:12-07:00","id":1552587,"title":"","content":"I agree with your perspective of canon.<br /> <br /> Gotta add, I find two main interpretations about it. First, knowing the preceding canon and work around it. Back in the day when Clanbook Toreador revised came out, it's history contradicted entirely everything, but I believe that was done on purpose. This sparked a lot of arguments on the old white-wolf forums back in the day. Another example is V20's Beckett's Jyhad Diary from &quot;The Dead Walk&quot; chapter. Here the Baron Samedi (the NPC, not the forum user, his reviews were the best!) misdirects his origins to Beckett and Talley which they immediately see through his bullshit. All this is done intentionally, done knowing a prime canon lore above it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, we have certain lore like Cretheus accounts from V20 The Black Hand in which many of his achievements and accounts come from before his embrace, which doesn't make any sense. Another example comes from Misery, childe of Marcus Vitel (from V5's Children of the Blood). She was embraced in 1962, Vancouver by Marcus Vitel. That would be extremely unlikely since Marcus Vitel recently awaken from torpor in a Maryland plantation. To have him go to Vancouver and have this feud with Prince Siegfried I'd say is just not considering the whole picture of the canon lore. My point here being, there are some canon alterations masquerading just because those who write it ignore what is previously done. From the writers perspective if misinterpretations are pointed out, they'd simply point it out later as the &quot;Cainites usually gives inconsistent stories&quot; excuse (don't get me wrong, I really liked Misery's story!).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}